## Story Description
Add two analytical columns to the Category Fragmentation Scorecard table: Avg Invoice Size (total_spend / transaction_count) and Spend Density (total_spend / supplier_count, i.e. average spend per supplier). These metrics help a category manager immediately assess whether a category is dominated by a few large invoices or fragmented across many small ones.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/CategoryPage.tsx
- In the Fragmentation Scorecard table (the Table rendered when selectedL1Entry is null), add two new TableHead columns after 'Suppliers': 'Avg Invoice' and 'Spend / Supplier'.
- For each row in the scorecard, compute: avgInvoice = entry.total_spend / Math.max(entry.transaction_count, 1), spendPerSupplier = entry.total_spend / Math.max(entry.supplier_count, 1).
- Render both as text-right TableCell using formatCurrency(). For avgInvoice: if > 50000 add className='text-right font-medium text-amber-600' (large average invoice — worth noting). For spendPerSupplier: no special colouring.
- Add TableHead for both columns with className='text-right'.
- Ensure the existing columns (L1 Category, Total Spend, % of Total, Suppliers, Status) remain in the same order — new columns appear after Suppliers.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

